Privacy Policy for "AI Chatbot"
Effective Date: December 30, 2025

This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, and share information when you interact with our application, "AI Chatbot", which integrates with the 
Meta Platform via the WhatsApp Business API.

1. Information We Collect
To provide automated chat services, we access certain information via Meta APIs (the "Platform Data"). This occurs when you initiate a conversation with our 
chatbot or grant permission through a Meta-authorized entry point.
Contact Information: Your WhatsApp phone number (required to route messages) and your WhatsApp profile name.
Messaging Content: We process the text, images, or media you send to the chatbot to generate AI responses. We also store timestamps and message status 
(sent/delivered/read) for service optimization.
User-Provided Data: Any information you voluntarily share during a chat session (e.g., email address or account details provided to the AI for support).
What we DO NOT collect: We do not access your private WhatsApp contact list, your personal status updates, or messages sent to other people/groups 
outside of this specific chat.

2. How We Use Your Information
We use your data strictly to provide the AI Chatbot's core functionality, including:
Processing your inquiries and providing AI-generated responses.
Personalizing the chat experience based on your previous interactions (where permitted).
Maintaining a log of your conversation history so you can resume chats later.
Analyzing chatbot performance to improve AI accuracy.
We do not sell your personal data or messaging content to third parties.

3. Data Retention and Deletion
We only retain Platform Data for as long as necessary to provide the services you requested.
User-Requested Deletion: You may request the deletion of your data at any time by contacting us at digitalbaku994@gmail.com.
Automatic Deletion: We periodically purge conversation logs that are older than 90 days unless retention is required for active service.
Meta Compliance: We comply with Meta’s Platform Terms. Upon a valid deletion request, we will remove your associated data from our servers within 30 days.
Data Deletion Instructions
"AI Chatbot" provides a transparent way for you to request the deletion of any data collected from your WhatsApp interaction.

Step 1: Opt-Out of Messaging
To stop receiving messages and revoke our app's ability to contact you:
Open the chat with "AI Chatbot" in WhatsApp.
Tap the Business Name at the top.
Scroll down and select Block Business or Report & Block.

Step 2: Request Permanent Data Deletion
To permanently delete your chat logs and phone number from our database, choose one of the following:
Email Request: Send an email to digitalbaku994@gmail.com with the subject "WhatsApp Data Deletion." You must include the phone number 
(in international format, e.g., +994...) used to interact with the bot.


Step 3: Confirmation
If requested via email, we will send a confirmation once your data has been purged. Please note that once deleted, your chat history with the 
AI cannot be recovered.

4. Sharing of Information
We only share your information in these limited circumstances:
With Meta: To transmit messages through the WhatsApp Business Platform.
AI Processors: We may process your text through secure AI models (e.g., OpenAI or Meta Llama) to generate responses. These providers do not use 
your data to train their global models when sent via our secure API.
Legal Requirements: If required by law or to protect the safety of our users.

5. Security and Encryption
WhatsApp messages are protected by end-to-end encryption between your device and the WhatsApp Business API. 
Once received by our App:
We use SSL/TLS encryption for all data in transit.
Stored data is protected using AES-256 encryption.

